Negative seven is at most two x minus
three, which is at most seven. So negative

25
00:02:03,927 --> 00:02:06,885
two is at most x, which is at most five.

26
00:02:08,033 --> 00:02:12,513
Before we add a third variable, let's
review systems in two variables.

27
00:02:13,633 --> 00:02:18,646
You can solve a system by graphing, by
substitution, or by elimination.

28
00:02:19,096 --> 00:02:24,515
Graphing shows the picture. Substitution
and elimination give exact answers.

29
00:02:25,633 --> 00:02:32,140
Solve y equals three x minus five, and two
x plus y equals ten, by substitution.

30
00:02:32,590 --> 00:02:39,400
Two x plus three x minus five equals ten,
so five x equals fifteen, and x equals

31
00:02:39,400 --> 00:02:41,614
three. Then y equals four.

32
00:02:42,733 --> 00:02:48,762
Solve four x plus three y equals
seventeen, and two x minus three y equals

33
00:02:48,762 --> 00:02:50,392
one, by elimination.

34
00:02:50,842 --> 00:02:57,172
Add the equations: six x equals eighteen,
so x equals three. Then three y equals

35
00:02:57,172 --> 00:02:59,546
five, so y equals five thirds.

36
00:03:00,666 --> 00:03:02,586
Remember the three possibilities.

37
00:03:03,036 --> 00:03:08,190
One solution where the lines cross. No
solution when they're parallel. Infinitely

38
00:03:08,190 --> 00:03:10,226
