49
00:03:59,566 --> 00:04:05,113
An equation like x plus y plus z equals
six describes a plane in space.

50
00:04:05,563 --> 00:04:10,406
A solution of three such equations is a
point where all three planes meet.

51
00:04:11,533 --> 00:04:17,272
The strategy is to use elimination twice
to remove the same variable. That leaves

52
00:04:17,272 --> 00:04:19,469
two equations in two variables.

53
00:04:19,919 --> 00:04:24,698
Solve that smaller system, then substitute
back to find the third variable.

54
00:04:25,833 --> 00:04:33,060
Solve x plus y plus z equals six, two x
minus y plus z equals three, and x plus

55
00:04:33,060 --> 00:04:35,348
two y minus z equals two.

56
00:04:35,798 --> 00:04:41,915
Add the first and third: two x plus three
y equals eight. Add the second and third:

57
00:04:41,915 --> 00:04:43,904
three x plus y equals five.

58
00:04:45,033 --> 00:04:50,750
Now solve two x plus three y equals eight,
and three x plus y equals five.

59
00:04:51,200 --> 00:04:57,679
Multiply the second by three: nine x plus
three y equals fifteen. Subtract the

60
00:04:57,679 --> 00:05:02,912
